      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבַשׁ</span></big><sub>54</sub>  <strong>substantivo masculino.</strong> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:29\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.29\">1Sm 14.29</a> mel <strong>(</strong>denominado pela cor segundo Fl NHWB<sup>i. 439</sup>; árabe <span dir=\"rtl\">دِبْسٌ</span> (<span dir=\"rtl\">دُبْسٌ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">دِبِسٌ</span>) <em>mel de tâmaras;</em> hebraico novo <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבַשׁ</span>, aramaico <span dir=\"rtl\">דּובשא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܕܒܰܫ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܕܶܒܫܳܐ</span>, <em>mel</em> tanto de frutos como de abelhas; cf. também assírio <em>dišpu</em> COT<sup>Gloss.</sup> Zim<sup>BP 84</sup> Dl<sup>Pr 70</sup><strong>)</strong>—absoluto <span dir=\"rtl\">ד׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 43:11\" href=\"/Genesis.43.11\">Gn 43.11</a> + 33 vezes; <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבָ֑שׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 3:8\" href=\"/Exodus.3.8\">Êx 3.8</a> + 18 vezes; com sufixo <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּבְשִׁי</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.1\">Ct 5.1</a>;—<em>mel</em>, produto das abelhas, usado como alimento <a data-ref=\"Judges 14:8\" href=\"/Judges.14.8\">Jz 14.8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 14:9\" href=\"/Judges.14.9\">Jz 14.9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 14:18\" href=\"/Judges.14.18\">Jz 14.18</a> (na carcaça do leão); encontrado em (fendas de) rocha <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 32:13\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.32.13\">Dt 32.13</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ד׳ מִסֶּלַע</span>, em cântico, JE), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 81:17\" href=\"/Psalms.81.17\">Sl 81.17</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(מִצּוּר ד׳)</span>; no bosque, sobre o solo <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:25\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.25\">1Sm 14.25</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(על־פני השׂדה)</span> v. <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:26\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.26\">1Sm 14.26</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">הֵלֶךְ ד׳</span>; mas leia-se antes <span dir=\"rtl\">הָלַךְ דְּבֹרוֹ</span> <em>suas abelhas haviam partido</em>, We Dr segundo 𝔊) v. <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:29\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.29\">1Sm 14.29</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:43\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.43\">1Sm 14.43</a>; transportado em jarro ou garrafa <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּקְבֻּק ד׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 14:3\" href=\"/I_Kings.14.3\">1Rs 14.3</a>; contribuição aos sacerdotes e levitas <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 31:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.31.5\">2Cr 31.5</a>; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">חֶמְאָה</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:29\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.29\">2Sm 17.29</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:15\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.15\">Is 7.15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:22\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.22\">Is 7.22</a> (nos últimos dois casos, a limitação a tal alimento é aparentemente sinal de indigência); conservado em reserva <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 41:8\" href=\"/Jeremiah.41.8\">Jr 41.8</a>; presente escolhido <a data-ref=\"Genesis 43:11\" href=\"/Genesis.43.11\">Gn 43.11</a> (J); artigo de comércio <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.17\">Ez 27.17</a> (nestes dois casos talvez = <em>xarope de uvas</em>, moderno <em>dibs</em>, cf. Di <a data-ref=\"Genesis 43:11\" href=\"/Genesis.43.11\">Gn 43.11</a> ver Rob<sup>BR ii. 81</sup>); proibido como oferta queimada <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 2:11\" href=\"/Leviticus.2.11\">Lv 2.11</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׂאֹר</span>); <em>favo de mel</em> = <span dir=\"rtl\">יַעְרַת הַדּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:27\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.27\">1Sm 14.27</a> (cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יַעְרִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.1\">Ct 5.1</a>); também <span dir=\"rtl\">צוּף ד׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 16:24\" href=\"/Proverbs.16.24\">Pv 16.24</a> (cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">נֹפֶת צופים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 19:11\" href=\"/Psalms.19.11\">Sl 19.11</a>); mais frequentemente na expressão que descreve a abundância na terra de Canaã <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ זָבַת חָלָב וּד׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 3:8\" href=\"/Exodus.3.8\">Êx 3.8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 3:17\" href=\"/Exodus.3.17\">Êx 3.17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 13:5\" href=\"/Exodus.13.5\">Êx 13.5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 33:3\" href=\"/Exodus.33.3\">Êx 33.3</a> (todos JE) <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 20:24\" href=\"/Leviticus.20.24\">Lv 20.24</a> (H) <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:27\" href=\"/Numbers.13.27\">Nm 13.27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 14:8\" href=\"/Numbers.14.8\">Nm 14.8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 16:14\" href=\"/Numbers.16.14\">Nm 16.14</a> (todos JE) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 6:3\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.6.3\">Dt 6.3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 11:9\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.11.9\">Dt 11.9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 26:9\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.26.9\">Dt 26.9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 26:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.26.15\">Dt 26.15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 27:3\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.27.3\">Dt 27.3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 31:20\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.31.20\">Dt 31.20</a> (todos D) <a data-ref=\"Joshua 5:6\" href=\"/Joshua.5.6\">Js 5.6</a> (D) <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 11:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.11.5\">Jr 11.5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 32:22\" href=\"/Jeremiah.32.22\">Jr 32.22</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 20:6\" href=\"/Ezekiel.20.6\">Ez 20.6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 20:15\" href=\"/Ezekiel.20.15\">Ez 20.15</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 8:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.8.8\">Dt 8.8</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 18:32\" href=\"/II_Kings.18.32\">2Rs 18.32</a> (da terra do cativeiro), do Egito <a data-ref=\"Numbers 16:13\" href=\"/Numbers.16.13\">Nm 16.13</a> (JE); ver também <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:13\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.13\">Ez 16.13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:19\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.19\">Ez 16.19</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 20:17\" href=\"/Job.20.17\">Jó 20.17</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">נַחֲלֵי ד׳ וְחֶמְאָה</span>; <em>mel</em>, usado para ilustrar ensinamentos morais <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 24:13\" href=\"/Proverbs.24.13\">Pv 24.13</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">נֹפֶת</span>), <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 25:16\" href=\"/Proverbs.25.16\">Pv 25.16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 25:27\" href=\"/Proverbs.25.27\">Pv 25.27</a> (perigo de saciedade excessiva); símile da doçura do sabor <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:3\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.3\">Ez 3.3</a> (do rolo), cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּצַפִּיחִת בִּד׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:31\" href=\"/Exodus.16.31\">Êx 16.31</a> (P; descrição do maná); da doçura da lei <a data-ref=\"Psalms 19:11\" href=\"/Psalms.19.11\">Sl 19.11</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">נֹפֶת צוּפִים</span>) cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 119:103\" href=\"/Psalms.119.103\">Sl 119.103</a>; (de palavras agradáveis <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 16:24\" href=\"/Proverbs.16.24\">Pv 16.24</a> cf. acima); doçura dos lábios <span dir=\"rtl\">ד׳ וְחָלָב</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:11\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.11\">Ct 4.11</a>; figura do amor <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּבְשִׁי</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.1\">Ct 5.1</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">יַעְרִי</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">יֵינִי</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">חֲלָבִי</span>).",
